From 677f512e1230f91df3391ef63d2020aebd380568 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:21:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(kanban):=20cross-gateway=20capability=20ro?=
 =?UTF-8?q?uting=20=E2=80=94=20a=20wall=20opens=20an=20owner=20card=20wher?=
 =?UTF-8?q?e=20the=20capability=20lives=20[daveey]?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hub workers hit walls another gateway could clear in minutes (hub IAM role lacked EC2
Describe 10-26 02:03-23:56 PT while the MacBook held AWS SSO admin; later EC2 mutation,
GetConsoleOutput, ssh to the mini). kind='assignment' only reaches a same-gateway supervisor
that lacks the capability too, so the cards parked on probes nobody was producing.

- kanban_capability_registry: each gateway live-checks its capabilities (config probes such as
  `aws sts get-caller-identity --profile ...`, ssh BatchMode reachability, sudo -n, gh login and
  scopes) off-thread from the dispatcher tick and writes kanban/capabilities.json (names, ok,
  checked_at; no commands or output). hermes-hub >= 1.6.2 publishes it as the `capabilities`
  collection; lookups trust only entries checked within stale_after_seconds.
- kanban_capability_routing: kanban_block/kanban_schedule take optional `needs`
  (CLI --need). When this gateway lacks a need and another holds it fresh, ONE owner card is
  created there via `hermes-hub create-task <gw> ... --id capability-owner:<card>:<need>`
  (scoped action, readback, wake; the owner card, not the worker, files any human_request),
  and the card parks scheduled on `hermes kanban wait-check capability-owner <request ids>`.
  Typed refusals, nothing written: no_capability_holder (points at human_request),
  capability_registry_stale, capability_held_locally, capability_route_exhausted.
- Placement preflight: namespaced gateway needs in `requires` pass through profile validation
  (PR47 validate_assignment) and are pre-routed at creation.
